From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duke Eagleman <301139544+jerricky26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:08:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: bluetooth: brcm: Add apple,wlan

Apple fits the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth combo modules of its phones and
tablets from more than one vendor (Murata, USI), and the Bluetooth
Patchram differs per vendor. The controller's ROM doesn't report the
vendor; only the Wi-Fi function's OTP does. Add a phandle from the
Bluetooth node to the Wi-Fi function of the same module, so that the
Patchram can follow the vendor the Wi-Fi driver read.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/net/bluetooth/brcm,bluetooth.yaml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/bluetooth/brcm,bluetooth.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/bluetooth/brcm,bluetooth.yaml
index b815e3615567..793857de0daa 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/bluetooth/brcm,bluetooth.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/bluetooth/brcm,bluetooth.yaml
@@ -122,6 +122,14 @@ properties:
       if the device's initial baud rate in normal mode is not supported by the
       host or if the device requires autobaud mode startup before loading FW.
 
+  apple,wlan:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The Wi-Fi function of the same Apple module. Apple fits modules from
+      several vendors, each needing its own Patchram, and only the Wi-Fi
+      function can read the module vendor from its OTP. The Patchram is
+      chosen by the vendor that the Wi-Fi driver reads.
+
   interrupts:
     items:
       - description: Handle to the line HOST_WAKE used to wake
